<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
    Custom item icons, and the one thing a Custom Game must switch on for them:
    "custom_icons": true in description.json. Without that flag this file is
    never read, and NOTlift falls back to a render of its previewRenderable,
    which is the LIFT's. It would look exactly like the thing it replaces.

    Format taken from the corpus rather than guessed: 31 Workshop items ship
    custom_icons and every one is a Gui/IconMap.xml plus Gui/IconMap.png pair in
    this exact shape. 2809564171 "Portal Gun [Game Mode]" is the closest
    precedent, being a Custom Game like this one. Vanilla's own is
    Data/Gui/IconMap.xml, a 2048x1024 atlas on the same 96x96 grid.

    NOTE FOR ANYONE EDITING THIS FILE: an XML comment may not contain two
    hyphens in a row. The first draft of this header used them as dashes the way
    the Lua files do, and the result was a file the parser rejected outright.
    dev/check_uuids.py caught it on its first run; the game would not have said
    anything at all.

    THE ATLAS IS 384x128 AND TILE 0,0 IS DELIBERATELY EMPTY.

    Every mod in the corpus declares an "Empty" index pointing at 0 0, and every
    one also puts its first real icon there, so "Empty" resolves to a picture.
    That is probably harmless, but it is a guess about what the engine asks
    "Empty" for, and the cost of being wrong is a crossed out lift turning up
    wherever it asks. Vanilla's own tile at 0,0 is a wood block, which suggests
    "Empty" is a name that happens to sit there rather than the blank slot
    graphic.

    So the index is declared, because 20 of 20 files declare it, and it points
    at a genuinely transparent tile. The icon lives at 96 0. One extra 96 pixels
    of texture buys not having to be right about it.
-->
<MyGUI type="Resource" version="1.1">
    <Resource type="ResourceImageSet" name="ItemIconsSet0">
        <Group name="ItemIcons" texture="IconMap.png" size="96 96">
            <Index name="Empty">
                <Frame point="0 0"/>
            </Index>
            <!-- NOTlift: the creative lift's own icon, crossed out. It is the
                 lift menu you want and it is not a lift, and the icon says both
                 at a glance. Cropped from Data/Gui/IconMap.png at 1056,768,
                 which is where that file maps uuid 5cc12f03. -->
            <Index name="7b3d5c91-4a2e-4f88-9c17-2e6d0b5a13ff">
                <Frame point="96 0"/>
            </Index>
            <!-- The Cleaner: survival's sledgehammer icon, crossed out. It IS a
                 sledgehammer subclass and it looks like one in the hand, so
                 without this it is indistinguishable from the real hammer in the
                 menu. Cropped from Survival/Gui/IconMapSurvival.png at
                 1728,2496, where that file maps uuid bb641a4f. -->
            <Index name="bbbb0cc8-5dd0-46e1-9299-8080c3cc80db">
                <Frame point="192 0"/>
            </Index>
            <!-- The Focus tool: the very marker it puts over a player, which is
                 $GAME_DATA/Gui/QuestMarker/icon_questmarker.png scaled to the
                 grid. It is a Sledgehammer subclass like the Cleaner and draws
                 the sledgehammer preview, so without this the two would be
                 indistinguishable in the menu, and both would look like the
                 real hammer. -->
            <Index name="f0c5a11e-7d3b-4c6a-9e21-5b8a4d0f9c33">
                <Frame point="288 0"/>
            </Index>
        </Group>
    </Resource>
</MyGUI>
